                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]I hate when such things happen in a game![/h1]\n\nFirst I have to note this game is a hidden object game title, it's about a police officer who is living a double existence as a ruthless costumed and masked thief. Well, that's in general most of the story that is to this game.\n\nAs player you can just be glad and happy it has no achievements, since this game is - well not exactly bad, but it also isn't a very good game of the genre - there are some riddles and puzzles that can give you quite the headache. I like hard puzzles, I like games where all isn't quite obvious - but I also like a barrier-free gaming experience. This isn't given all the time on that game.\n\nThe game is missing a lot of stuff, professional voice acting is non existent and the story is very rudimentary developed and highly illogical at times...\n\nPro:[list][*]Good to excelent graphics.[*]Nice and stylish soundtrack.[*]Some inovative riddles.[/list]\nCon:[list][*]The story isn't logical and sometimes it's outright a mess.[*]The game is sometimes unclear about the directions and steps required to solve a given riddle, partially this is frustrating and you might give it to the overburdened scenes.[*]No Voiceacting.[*]Sometimes too restrictive in the placing of objects, which also might get on your nerves if you have to retry placing something half a dozen times...[*] Far too expensive. [/list]\n\n[h1]Not Recommended[/h1]\n\nGiven some of the graphics in this game are outright excelent, especially some of the scenes for the hidden objects, the game in itself is a lot of frustration and the story itself is cheesy - if you want to call it this way. The price is also a big minus and if it hasn't been in a bundle I probably wouldn't have bothered. You can call yourself lucky this game has no achievements, you would be forced to run through a game that's mostly time and money robbery - oh... That reminds me on the Title... Black Viper is a thief, isn't she? At least she wasn't able to steal my heart.",
